 installation, not about the clone; --omp-binary/--opencode-binary override both
 for fixture runs.
+
+Substrates are resolution chains, not files (round 47, the npx-wrapper install
+shape). `omp` is a plain file. `opencode` is NOT: since the host's opencode
+became an npx wrapper, `~/.local/bin/opencode` is a bash script that resolves
+the package bin inside the npm npx cache and execs it, so the artifact that
+actually runs is
+
+  <npm cache>/_npx/<sha512(spec)[:16]>/node_modules/.bin/<bin>   (a symlink)
+    -> .../node_modules/<pkg>/bin/<bin>                          (the ELF)
+
+with `spec` the `--package` string the wrapper names (npm derives the _npx
+directory name from it: libnpmexec/lib/index.js hashes the requested spec
+strings with sha512 and keeps the first 16 hex characters). The directory
+therefore stays stable across releases of the same spec: a new upstream
+version replaces the bytes IN PLACE, which the sha256 pin sees. A change of
+spec, of install method, or of the npm cache root moves the resolution -- and
+those are the events that used to leave this guard GREEN while the live
+substrate was a different binary. The contract therefore pins the launcher as
+a substrate of its own (`opencode_launcher_binary_sha256`): the launcher
+carries the premise of the artifact path, so a re-pointed launcher, a
+replaced wrapper, or a removed wrapper is DRIFT/UNREADABLE (exit 1/2), never a
+silent pass. Re-pinning the opencode artifact means re-deriving its path from
+the launcher and re-recording BOTH the artifact sha and the launcher sha,
+plus a mechanism note (what moved and why) -- never weakening a pin.
+
+The discovery rule is fail-closed over the whole pin-shaped key space: any
+`measured_against` key shaped `<substrate>_binary_<kind>` is DISCOVERED
+(including a compound kind with underscores, which the round-32 regex
+excluded and therefore silently ignored -- the round-21 "unenforced pin" class
+reopened inside the discovery rule itself), and a discovered key the guard
+cannot resolve is UNSUPPORTED (exit 2), never a silent skip.
 """
 
